# Keystatic CMS — GitHub storage mode (ADR-0009).
#
# These power the GitHub-App OAuth flow that lets the Netlify-hosted admin
# (/keystatic) commit straight to this repo. They are required ONLY for the
# Netlify deploy and for cloud editing during local dev; the GitHub Pages
# build ships no admin and ignores them.
#
# DO NOT commit real values. Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored)
# for local use, and set the same three vars in the Netlify dashboard
# (Site settings → Environment variables) for production.
#
# How to obtain them: create a GitHub App (see docs/adr/0009-cms-keystatic.md).
#   - CLIENT_ID / CLIENT_SECRET come from that GitHub App.
#   - KEYSTATIC_SECRET is any random 32+ char string you generate, e.g.
#       openssl rand -hex 32

KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
KEYSTATIC_SECRET=
